    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on a high-ceiling core today, led by **Gunnar Henderson**, who at an 83.29 rating is our clear priority start against Flaherty. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a favorable park environment (+16%) and a strong platoon advantage, making him the anchor of our lineup. Following closely is **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, boasting a 72.21 rating; his placement in the two-hole against Elder offers a prime opportunity to drive scoring efficiency. Additionally, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains a must-start at 62.64, as his elite peripheral metrics (xwOBA of .376) help him navigate the challenge of facing Chandler, despite the minor downward pressure from the platoon dynamic.\n\nThe decision-making process was particularly difficult regarding **Sam Antonacci** and **Nolan Schanuel**. **Sam Antonacci** nearly cracked the starting nine with a 44.85 rating, bolstered by a potential lead-off role and favorable winds, but the optimizer ultimately prioritized the superior efficiency of **Gage Workman** and **Andy Pages** in their respective spots. Meanwhile, **Josh Jung** is an intriguing play at 63.73; he draws a favorable matchup against Grayson Rodriguez, who carries a shaky 5.91 xERA. **Kyle Tucker** and **Josh Lowe** remain in the lineup despite the inherent risk of facing high-caliber arms like Henderson and deGrom; specifically, **Josh Lowe** receives a small boost from the platoon advantage, but we must monitor his production closely as the elite strikeout rate of deGrom presents a significant floor risk. \n\nAs we approach first pitch, the uncertainty surrounding lineup positioning for **Josh Jung**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Josh Lowe**\u2014all of whom were projected based on \"Lineup Pending\" status\u2014introduces some volatility. If any of these three drop significantly in the order, their efficiency scores will likely see a downward adjustment. We are effectively betting on the offensive environments of these games to offset the SP skill displayed by the opposing starters, particularly in the case of **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker**, who face the toughest pitching opposition of the day.",
